        "controller_support": "full",
        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>GRIBOUILLE is an exploration game that takes place entirely inside my sketchbook.</strong> <br>For hundreds of days, I drew one page every single day. Today, those pages have become a world you can explore.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a small character wandering through my sketchbook, page after page. <br>Every page you collect is a piece of my learning journey, and also a <strong>checkpoint</strong> that helps you progress through this scattered notebook you must piece back together.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And more importantly: <strong>you can draw directly inside the world of the game.</strong> <br>Just like in a real sketchbook, you’re free to doodle, annotate, scribble, or leave your own marks.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A poetic exploration adventure</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No enemies, no combat. <br>GRIBOUILLE is an artistic walk, a game where you look around, discover, climb, wander… and sometimes get lost. <br>It plays like visiting an art exhibition, but inside a 2D world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Collection &amp; progression</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each page you find:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >becomes a checkpoint</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >represents one day from my year-long learning process</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >can unlock a new ability</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>300 original drawings</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All taken from my 300-day daily drawing challenge. <br>Every page comes with a small piece of story.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>GRIBOUILLE is an art exhibition turned into a video game.</strong> <br>It is a contemplative, poetic, and personal experience where you explore a sketchbook the way you would explore an art gallery… but with the freedom of a platformer.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>GRIBOUILLE is an exploration game that takes place entirely inside my sketchbook.</strong> <br>For hundreds of days, I drew one page every single day. Today, those pages have become a world you can explore.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a small character wandering through my sketchbook, page after page. <br>Every page you collect is a piece of my learning journey, and also a <strong>checkpoint</strong> that helps you progress through this scattered notebook you must piece back together.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And more importantly: <strong>you can draw directly inside the world of the game.</strong> <br>Just like in a real sketchbook, you’re free to doodle, annotate, scribble, or leave your own marks.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A poetic exploration adventure</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No enemies, no combat. <br>GRIBOUILLE is an artistic walk, a game where you look around, discover, climb, wander… and sometimes get lost. <br>It plays like visiting an art exhibition, but inside a 2D world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Collection &amp; progression</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each page you find:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >becomes a checkpoint</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >represents one day from my year-long learning process</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >can unlock a new ability</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>300 original drawings</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All taken from my 300-day daily drawing challenge. <br>Every page comes with a small piece of story.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>GRIBOUILLE is an art exhibition turned into a video game.</strong> <br>It is a contemplative, poetic, and personal experience where you explore a sketchbook the way you would explore an art gallery… but with the freedom of a platformer.</p>",
        "short_description": "GRIBOUILLE is an exploration game set inside my sketchbook. You travel through the pages I drew every day for a year. It’s a simple, personal little adventure where I share my drawing journey through a 2D platformer.",
